    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d677">

                <pb facs="0759" n="747" sameAs="frus:frus1940v03/pg747"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.90G21/3: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister Resident in Iraq</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Knabenshue</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Baghdad</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-01-29T10:00:00+03:00">January 29,
                            1940—10 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received January 29—9:40 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>8. With reference to my telegram No. 1, January 2, 10 a.m.,<anchor n="38"
                        xml:id="d677-f1"/> I am now in receipt of an official communication from the
                    Foreign Office expressing willingness of the Iraqi Government to conclude
                    consular convention with the United States and desire to receive draft
                    proposals.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Knabenshue</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
